/T (Strain is highly responsive to the wider environment, shifting with regional conditions, seasonal factors such as the summer holiday period, and concerns about AI and job security. This makes strain an important indicator of how employees are responding to changes around them, rather than simply an internal workplace measure. The level and volatility of strain highlight the need for regular monitoring and targeted support to identify emerging pressures before they affect wellbeing, engagement and retention.)
