<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 121 0 R
/T (83% of employees use AI tools provided by their employer, and more than half use them weekly. But adoption is uneven, and clarity plus capability make the difference.)
/E (83% of employees use AI tools provided by their employer, and more than half use them weekly. But adoption is uneven, and clarity plus capability make the difference.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
658 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/P 121 0 R
/T (Access alone does not drive adoption. At the front line, the barrier is access to AI tools; amongst managers, it is reluctance to use tools that are already available. In both cases, clarity and skills are key, but the needs differ across the organisation. Investing in capability, not just technology, is what turns AI from a source of concern into a source of competitive value.)
/E (Access alone does not drive adoption. At the front line, the barrier is access to AI tools; amongst managers, it is reluctance to use tools that are already available. In both cases, clarity and skills are key, but the needs differ across the organisation. Investing in capability, not just technology, is what turns AI from a source of concern into a source of competitive value.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
